WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:10.020
The 5G wireless transformation requires
the right frequencies. Now, low-band radio

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.140
spectrum transmits small amounts of data
over long distances. The high-band transmits

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.660
large amount of data over short distances.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.300
Now, the mid-band spectrum — or so-called
"Goldilocks" frequencies, such as

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.500
the C-band — they have the right combination of
both properties, but it's in short supply.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.830
Now, 5G will allow wireless services to
carry more data faster. Using the C-band

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.240
is the fastest way to make 5G available
in as many places as possible.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.320
It's essential for US leadership to harmonize
devices with global 5G standards.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.420
Now, satellite operators have this C-band
spectrum and are willing to sell it

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.900
so it can be repurposed for 5G. But
seizing this opportunity depends upon

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:56.260
the FCC — the Federal Communications Commission.
It has to move quickly to hold a public auction in 2020.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:02.040
If the FCC fails to act or moves too slowly,
the US will lose the 5G race to China.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.000
5G innovation, investment, and jobs will go elsewhere.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.780
Should the US be the global leader in 5G
technologies? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.580
Also, let us know what other topics you'd
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:22.940
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for
more research and videos from AEI.

